# A function of its callee's own color held by a blueprint in the value a call returns,
# at a call that makes the color bounded (Type System ch. 5: a `u fn` takes its color
# from its call; ch. 2: a blueprint is an opaque handle and still a value, and `@ x` is
# the blueprint whose output is `x`; Semantics ch. 8: a blueprint builds nothing until a
# block applies it). Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

?Made: u fn (u fn Nat -> Nat) -> ?@(u fn Nat -> Nat)
fn ?Made F = ? @ F

@page: @unit
@page:
    match ?Made (\|n| n + 1):
        ? @T:
            F <- @T
            Ui.Label($text=$"{F 5}")
        nil: Ui.Label($text=$"none")
